  <script>
    (function() {
      const allReviews = [{"rating":3,"name":"Jasmine D.","location":"Atlanta, GA","tag":"Protective Styles • Braids","date":"3 days ago","title":"USPS crushed the package, but customer service was 10/10","text":"Package arrived with the outer box completely crushed by the mail carrier and a little oil had seeped past the foil seal. I emailed support with photos and they sent out a replacement the very next morning without giving me the runaround. The oil itself is thick, rich, and works wonders on my braided scalp."},{"rating":3,"name":"Brittany K.","location":"Detroit, MI","tag":"4C Coils • Traction Alopecia","date":"1 week ago","title":"Delivery took 8 days to Michigan","text":"The shipping was delayed through the regional distribution center and took over a week to arrive when tracking estimated 3 days. Almost canceled my order, but once it finally got here and I used it on my thinning temples, I understood the hype. Smells authentic and herbal, not like synthetic perfume."},{"rating":3,"name":"Danielle P.","location":"Philadelphia, PA","tag":"High Porosity • Dry Scalp","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"Lid was jammed shut, had to run under hot water","text":"Whoever sealed my jar tightened it with superhero strength, I literally had to run the lid under boiling water to twist it open. Once opened, the batana paste is lovely and melts instantly into my fingers. Sinks into my scalp without staining my silk pillowcase. Just wish the lid wasn't so stiff."},{"rating":4,"name":"Tamara J.","location":"Houston, TX","tag":"Thinning Hairline • 4B/4C","date":"4 days ago","title":"The oil is top tier, wish tracking was faster","text":"The oil itself is a solid 10/10. It melts into my scalp without leaving that suffocating grease film that mineral oils do. Docking one star because USPS tracking didn't update for three days straight between Dallas and Houston. But the product is genuine raw batana, edges are already looking darker."},{"rating":4,"name":"Alexis R.","location":"Chicago, IL","tag":"Postpartum Shedding","date":"1 week ago","title":"Strong earthy scent at first, but it works","text":"Be prepared for the smell — it has a roasted coffee-nut aroma that surprised me on night one. It fades after 20 minutes though, and after three weeks of nightly scalp massages, my postpartum thinning spots around my part are finally filling in with soft baby hairs. Definitely repurchasing."},{"rating":4,"name":"Monique B.","location":"Charlotte, NC","tag":"Knotless Braids • Scalp Care","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"Wish it came with a nozzle applicator","text":"Since it's in a jar, you have to scoop a small dime-sized amount with your fingertip. I really wish Zavelyn offered a pointed dropper bottle or mini spatula for getting directly between tight cornrows. That said, the batana soothes itchy braid tightness faster than any tea tree spray I've tried."},{"rating":4,"name":"Ebony T.","location":"Memphis, TN","tag":"Low Porosity • 4A Curls","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"Very thick in cold weather, warm it between hands","text":"When it arrived in cold November weather it was firm like cold butter. You have to rub it vigorously between your palms for 5 seconds to melt it into a silky golden oil. Once melted, my low porosity strands drink it up. My split ends feel noticeably sealed and hydrated."},{"rating":4,"name":"Kayla S.","location":"Dallas, TX","tag":"Edge Recovery • Slick Backs","date":"3 weeks ago","title":"Good results, just requires daily consistency","text":"You can't use this once a week and expect miracles. I had to commit to massaging it in every single night before tying my edges down with a satin wrap. By week 4, the bald patch from tight cheer ponytails was 70% covered in fuzzy new growth. It takes patience but it pays off."},{"rating":4,"name":"Tierra W.","location":"New Orleans, LA","tag":"Lace Wig Wearer","date":"3 weeks ago","title":"Saved my hairline from lace glue damage","text":"Years of ghost bond adhesive completely wrecked my perimeter. This oil gave my follicles a break. My hairline stopped tingling and peeling within 48 hours. Knocked off one star because the 120ml jar goes fast if you use it on your full scalp like I do. Need a larger 250ml size!"},{"rating":4,"name":"Destiny M.","location":"Baltimore, MD","tag":"4C Coils • Wash Day","date":"4 weeks ago","title":"Great pre-poo treatment","text":"I warm about a tablespoon in a bowl of warm water and use it as a pre-shampoo hot oil mask on wash days. My detangling session went from 45 minutes of crying and snapped combs down to 15 minutes of easy slip. Lost half a star on price, but the quality speaks for itself."},{"rating":5,"name":"Keisha M.","location":"Atlanta, GA","tag":"4C Coils • Knotless Braids","date":"1 day ago","title":"Baby hairs are finally showing after 6 months of nothing","text":"Listen, I was about to give up on my edges after wearing heavy knotless braids back to back all summer. Three weeks of massaging this into my temples every night before putting on my silk bonnet, and I finally see little dark baby hairs sprouting. It's thick, unrefined, and actually smells genuine."},{"rating":5,"name":"Aaliyah N.","location":"Brooklyn, NY","tag":"Traction Alopecia • 4A/4B","date":"2 days ago","title":"Real Batana, not that fake dyed coconut oil from Amazon","text":"I bought three different 'batana oils' on Amazon that turned out to be yellow petroleum and fragrance oil. Zavelyn is the real deal from Honduras. Rich dark amber paste, nutty smoky scent, and it doesn't leave a grey waxy film on dark scalps. My hairline is thanking me."},{"rating":5,"name":"Brianna C.","location":"Miami, FL","tag":"Heat Damage • 3C/4A","date":"2 days ago","title":"Restored my curl pattern around the crown","text":"The crown of my head was fried straight from years of silk presses. I've been doing nightly scalp massages with this oil for five weeks now. The new growth coming in is tight, juicy, and springing right back into coiled rings. My hair stylist asked me what I changed in my routine."},{"rating":5,"name":"Sonia G.","location":"Oakland, CA","tag":"4C Edges • Postpartum","date":"3 days ago","title":"Postpartum shedding stopped in its tracks","text":"Four months postpartum my hair was coming out in fistfuls in the shower drain and my corners were completely bare. This was recommended by my sister. Within three weeks the shedding slowed to normal, and by week six the bare spots had healthy dark fuzz. A total lifesaver."},{"rating":5,"name":"Courtney H.","location":"Orlando, FL","tag":"Dry Scalp • Itch Relief","date":"3 days ago","title":"Zero flakes under my sew-in weave","text":"Normally by week two of a sew-in, my scalp is burning, flaking, and itching like crazy. I warmed a dab of this in an applicator bottle and worked it down my braids. Instant relief. No build-up, no white gunk, just soothing pure botanical moisture. I won't install weaves without it."},{"rating":5,"name":"Zoe T.","location":"Richmond, VA","tag":"Crown Thinning • Menopause","date":"4 days ago","title":"My part line is finally narrowing down","text":"At 52, hormonal changes made my center part noticeably wide and see-through under bright bathroom lights. I apply this directly to the part line every other evening. Two months in, my part looks visibly denser and fuller. It doesn't weigh my fine textured coils down at all."},{"rating":5,"name":"Nia W.","location":"Washington, DC","tag":"Locs & Retwists","date":"4 days ago","title":"Keeps my loc roots hydrated and resilient","text":"I use this to palm roll my new growth and lubricate my scalp between retwist appointments. It leaves my locs with a healthy natural sheen without that stiff wax crust you get from beeswax or locking gels. Smells earthy and clean, pure ancestral hair food."},{"rating":5,"name":"Maya F.","location":"Chicago, IL","tag":"4C High Density","date":"5 days ago","title":"A little dab goes a very long way","text":"You really only need a dime-sized dollop for your whole perimeter. When you warm it between your fingers it liquefies into a velvety oil that absorbs in about five minutes. It doesn't migrate down your forehead while you sleep or cause forehead breakouts."},{"rating":5,"name":"Shanice L.","location":"Cleveland, OH","tag":"Tension Alopecia","date":"5 days ago","title":"My edges survived the holiday season","text":"I always stress out during the holidays with slick buns and back-to-back styling events. Using BotanaRoots as a nightly edge balm kept my hairline protected and strong. I noticed zero shedding on my edge brush. Truly miraculous stuff."},{"rating":5,"name":"Tiffany K.","location":"Los Angeles, CA","tag":"Color Treated • Bleached Curls","date":"6 days ago","title":"Revived my bleach-damaged coils","text":"Bleaching my 4B curls honey blonde left my strands brittle and snapping like dry twigs. Applying this oil as an overnight sealing treatment completely transformed my texture. My hair feels supple, retains water, and elasticity has returned. Worth every single penny."},{"rating":5,"name":"Kendra B.","location":"Jacksonville, FL","tag":"Edge Care • Silk Scarf Routine","date":"6 days ago","title":"Edges look like they did back in college","text":"I am 38 and my edges had thinned to the point where I refused to pull my hair into a high puff. After 40 days of consistent use with my silk scarf, the edges are full enough that I wore a sleek high ponytail to dinner last night. Felt so confident."},{"rating":5,"name":"Imani R.","location":"St. Louis, MO","tag":"Protective Braids","date":"1 week ago","title":"The only oil that doesn't trigger my scalp eczema","text":"Everything with added fragrance or essential oils gives me red itchy bumps along my hairline. Zavelyn's raw single-ingredient batana is so pure and clean that my sensitive scalp actually calms down. No flare-ups, no itching, just steady new growth."},{"rating":5,"name":"Latoya D.","location":"New York, NY","tag":"4C Tight Coils","date":"1 week ago","title":"Retention is real! Gained an inch in 2 months","text":"My issue was never growing hair, it was length retention because my 4C ends would snap off during detangling. Sealing my ends with this batana butter locked in the leave-in conditioner for days. Measured my length yesterday and I've retained over an inch of healthy new growth."},{"rating":5,"name":"Candace V.","location":"Newark, NJ","tag":"Edge Breakage","date":"1 week ago","title":"Visible difference under my headband","text":"I used to wear thick headbands to conceal the thinning gaps by my ears. Five weeks in, those sparse areas are completely shaded in with soft new hairs. It looks completely natural and blends right into my hairline. Will be setting up a subscription."},{"rating":5,"name":"Erica J.","location":"Indianapolis, IN","tag":"Transitioning to Natural","date":"1 week ago","title":"Smooth transition line without breakage","text":"Anyone who has transitioned from relaxers knows the line of demarcation snaps constantly. Massaging this oil onto the demarcation line gave my fragile strands the elasticity they needed to handle combing without snapping. Made my natural journey so much easier."},{"rating":5,"name":"Gabrielle M.","location":"Columbus, OH","tag":"Wash Day Routine","date":"1 week ago","title":"My favorite step in my Sunday wash day","text":"After deep conditioning, I apply this to my damp scalp and massage for five minutes with my silicone scalp scrubber. The tingling warmth is so relaxing. My scalp stays hydrated through the whole week until the next wash day without getting itchy or flaky."},{"rating":5,"name":"Taylor S.","location":"Austin, TX","tag":"Gym Goer • Sweat & Edges","date":"1 week ago","title":"Protects edges from constant sweat and drying","text":"I work out 5 days a week and sweat heavily. The salt from sweat used to dry out my hairline and snap my edges. Applying a tiny layer of this before working out acts like a water-resistant protective barrier. My edges stay supple and protected even after HIIT classes."},{"rating":5,"name":"Danielle H.","location":"Nashville, TN","tag":"Low Density Coils","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"Gives fine coils body and shine without limpness","text":"I have fine textured strands and most hair butters make my hair look greasy and flat against my head. This batana is lightweight once it melts down. My curls look fluffy, full of bounce, and reflect light beautifully."},{"rating":5,"name":"Chantel G.","location":"Milwaukee, WI","tag":"Winter Hair Protection","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"Midwest winter saver for dry brittle hair","text":"Wisconsin winters normally sap all moisture out of my hair within minutes of stepping outside. This oil seals in deep moisture like nothing else. My ends aren't crunchy and my edges aren't breaking from winter wool beanies."},{"rating":5,"name":"Raven E.","location":"Tampa, FL","tag":"4B/4C Coils","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"100% authentic Honduran batana texture","text":"My grandmother is from Central America and used to make batana by hand from the American palm nut. When I opened this jar and smelled that authentic roasted aroma, I knew immediately it was the real ancestral formula. Identical quality to what my family used."},{"rating":5,"name":"Dominique P.","location":"Kansas City, MO","tag":"Traction Edge Repair","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"Filled in the gap near my right temple","text":"My right side has always been thinner due to how I sleep. Four weeks of focused nightly massage with BotanaRoots and the gap is finally filling in. You can't even see the scalp through the hair anymore. So happy with these results."},{"rating":5,"name":"Krystal W.","location":"Birmingham, AL","tag":"Box Braids Maintenance","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"Kept my braids neat for two extra weeks","text":"Applying this to my parted lines every three days kept my scalp nourished and minimized frizz along the roots. I was able to keep my protective style looking salon-fresh for two weeks longer than usual, saving me money and time."},{"rating":5,"name":"Victoria C.","location":"Raleigh, NC","tag":"Sensitive Scalp","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"No synthetic chemicals or filler junk","text":"Read the ingredients: it is literally just 100% raw unrefined Elaeis Oleifera Kernel Oil. No petroleum, no mineral oil, no fake fragrance. That is why it works so well. My scalp absorbed it cleanly and my hair has never felt softer."},{"rating":5,"name":"Morgan B.","location":"San Antonio, TX","tag":"4C Coils • Scalp Health","date":"2 weeks ago","title":"Scalp feels breathing and refreshed","text":"I used to have constant buildup from heavy edge controls and gels. Replacing my edge control routine with this natural batana balm has been the best decision. My follicles are breathing and growing instead of being clogged with glue."},{"rating":5,"name":"Jada T.","location":"Memphis, TN","tag":"Alopecia Areata","date":"3 weeks ago","title":"Dermatologist was surprised at my checkup","text":"I brought this jar to my dermatologist after using it for six weeks on a quarter-sized spot on my crown. She inspected with a dermatoscope and confirmed healthy active follicle activity and new anagen growth. She told me to keep doing whatever I was doing!"},{"rating":5,"name":"Sierra M.","location":"Las Vegas, NV","tag":"Dry Desert Climate","date":"3 weeks ago","title":"Cured my desert dry scalp","text":"Living in Nevada dries out your skin and hair overnight. Since switching to this pure batana oil, my scalp has stopped itching completely. My hair holds onto moisture for three full days without re-misting. Essential product for dry climates."},{"rating":5,"name":"Chelsea D.","location":"Baltimore, MD","tag":"4A/4B Mixed Texture","date":"3 weeks ago","title":"The shine is unbeatable","text":"Most hair oils just sit on top of the cuticle looking greasy like grease paint. This oil actually penetrates into the hair shaft. My hair has that deep, healthy, lit-from-within sheen that lasts